<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <!--
      The app's calendar-and-clock mark, as a notification small icon.

      Notification small icons are drawn as a silhouette: the system throws away color and
      keeps only the alpha, then tints the result itself. That is why this is one flat white
      path with no tint attribute of its own — and why the pre-2.0 app's full-color PNG came
      out as a gray blob. It is also why the holes matter: the header line, the gap between
      the calendar and the clock, and the hands are the only things giving the silhouette any
      internal structure once it is flattened.

      Same path data as ic_launcher_foreground, re-fitted from that file's 108 viewport to
      this 24 one. The artwork spans (29,28)-(84.5,84.5) there, so scaling by 22/56.5 and
      shifting the result puts it in a 22dp box centered in the 24dp canvas — the inset a
      notification icon is expected to keep.
    -->
    <group
        android:scaleX="0.3894"
        android:scaleY="0.3894"
        android:translateX="-10.1"
        android:translateY="-9.9">
        <path
            android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
            android:fillType="evenOdd"
            android:pathData="M37,28 a2.5,2.5 0 0,1 2.5,2.5 v5 h-5 v-5 a2.5,2.5 0 0,1 2.5,-2.5 z
                              M55,28 a2.5,2.5 0 0,1 2.5,2.5 v5 h-5 v-5 a2.5,2.5 0 0,1 2.5,-2.5 z
                              M35,32 h24 a6,6 0 0,1 6,6 v27 a6,6 0 0,1 -6,6 h-24 a6,6 0 0,1 -6,-6 v-27 a6,6 0 0,1 6,-6 z
                              M29,43 h36 v4 h-36 z
